   136	
   137	## Threat model for the pre-handoff gate
   138	
   139	Pages are authored by Fannan or a human designer: honest but possibly sloppy, not an attacker. The gate must catch honest mistakes and ordinary authoring patterns completely (body or html clipping, zero-size or `display: contents` wrappers, open shadow roots, frames, objects and embeds, stylesheets loaded from `data:` or `blob:` URLs, state pages), and must fail closed on anything it cannot measure (closed shadow roots, unreadable or unserved stylesheets, frames, a vector field or native-function check that could not run, JavaScript-off content that is not equivalent).
   140	
   141	Deliberate obfuscation is outside the main threat model: for example JavaScript string escapes, comment tricks inside strings, patching `Function.prototype`, or base64-encoded stylesheets. Cheap defences are applied where they are simple (escapes are decoded and raw text is matched with and without comment stripping; the reduced-motion counter binds the native `requestAnimationFrame` at install and `call`/`apply`/`bind`/`Reflect.apply` are in the native-function check; `data:`/`blob:` stylesheets are refused). Anything beyond that is listed in `UNTESTED.md` as a known limit and is raised as ENH, not P0-P2, in future rounds. Defence in depth stays: computed-style checks, the JavaScript-off pass and the source scan.
   142	
   143	## Review convergence rule
   144	
   145	A review round passes when there are zero P0, P1 and P2 findings; P3 and ENH items are batched and don't block.
