| R14-GPT-04 | A | P2 | `release/tools/width-screen.mjs:132`; `release/tests/panel-r14.test.mjs:76` | “`['auto', 'scroll'].includes(getComputedStyle(a).overflowY)`” exempts content under any nominal scroller. Executed in-memory: hidden 900px viewport, auto-height `overflow-y:auto` wrapper with `clientHeight === scrollHeight === 1600`, text at y1550 → all failure arrays empty. The wrapper cannot scroll that text into view. Browser reproduction **UNVERIFIED**. Existing regression tests only a bounded `height:100%` scroller. | Exempt content only when its actual scroll range can bring it into the visible scrollport, accounting for viewport and ancestor clipping. Add 1440/320 browser regressions for an auto-height overflow wrapper and a scrollport extending below a hidden viewport; require FAIL while retaining the valid app-shell PASS case. |
| R14-GPT-06 | A | P2 | `scripts/package-r3.py:109`; `scripts/package-r3.py:111` | **N10/q2:** the content screen claims “any case or separator,” but executed in-memory JSON checks accept `Access_Token`, `accessToken` and `refreshToken` with 22-character dummy values. `credential_key()` recognizes all three. Thus ordinary `notes.json` can contain explicitly recognized credentials without rejection; these are not unknown-key limitations. | Apply the existing normalized credential-key policy recursively to JSON content in ordinary files, retaining the documented value threshold and non-JSON screening. Add package-input and changed-path regressions for these spellings; require rejection before outputs change. |
| R14-GPT-12 | A | P2 | `release/tools/integrity.mjs:64`; `release/tools/integrity.mjs:68` | **N12:** contrast composition ignores element/ancestor CSS `opacity`. Executed in-memory: black text on white, script changes opacity from `.1` to `1`; both probes return `contrastFailures:0`, `contrastUnknown:0`, `contrastChecked:1`, and integrity returns PASS. The JavaScript-off contrast is approximately 1.25:1. Browser reproduction **UNVERIFIED**. This is an ordinary reveal effect. | Correctly composite opacity through rendering groups, or mark affected required text unknown and fail the cross-check as INCOMPLETE. Add JavaScript-on/off browser regressions for element and ancestor opacity; both must fail without the fix. |
| R14-GPT-13 | B | P2 | `release/FANNAN-PLAN.md:61`; `release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:132`; `release/skills/design-prototype/SKILL.md:12` | “Run the wireframe phase … **before Step 5**,” but new required IDs `navigation-findability` and `task-test` require Step 5 testing/retests (`FANNAN-PLAN.md:51,67`). Only accent/palette may be DEFERRED. R14-GPT-08/11 therefore make the prescribed Step 4 exit require future evidence. | Replace the scheduling rule with: “At Step 4, check grayscale structure, copy and provenance and record issues for testing. Within the existing Step 5 gate, after task and navigation-findability tests and necessary retests, run the complete wireframe quality gate. Require PASS before structure approval and Step 6.” Align the prototype caller and repeated scheduling guidance; preserve all nine steps. |
| R14-GPT-14 | B | P2 | `release/FANNAN-PLAN.md:77`; `release/tools/token-references.mjs:43` | R14-MIMAR-05 requires “column count, gutter, outer margin, maximum content width … **each value is a spacing-scale token**.” Spacing tokens require dimensions with units; a column count requires a unitless integer. The new instruction conflicts with the token contract and owner’s units rule. | Replace that clause with: “Column counts are positive unitless integers recorded separately from spacing tokens. Gutters, outer margins and maximum content widths reference approved dimension tokens with units; bare zero is permitted and negative spacing tokens are refused. Document recomposition as behavior.” |
| R14-GPT-15 | B | P2 | `release/references/handoff-contract.md:24`; `release/runtime/quality-checks.json:23`; `release/tests/handoff-contract.test.mjs:31` | R14-MIMAR-01 requires “the approver’s feedback log with every item resolved or explicitly deferred,” but no required manual ID or validator field checks it. The existing “complete handoff passes” fixture omits feedback evidence and asserts no errors. The new document test checks wording only. | Add required manual ID `feedback-log`. In `design-quality.md`, add: “The feedback-log artifact records scoped feedback, interpretation, resulting versions and confirmation for every item. Deferral requires the approver’s recorded disposition and leaves no unresolved handoff question or BLOCK defect. Missing or unresolved coverage fails. If no feedback was received, record that explicitly with reviewer and scope.” Add missing/failed-review regressions through the existing manual-check validator. |

